      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#37662 pinned MP4 encoding to the static ffmpeg bundled with `imageio-ffmpeg`, so outputs stay reproducible. That makes sense as the default. On some CPUs, though, the bundled build (ffmpeg 4.2.2) is much slower than a recent ffmpeg, and the docs do not say how to opt out.\n\nOn an aarch64 host (8x RTX 5090, LTX-2.5 T2V, 960x544, 121 frames, `--x264-preset fast`), the two binaries took this long per video with the same arguments:\n\n| ffmpeg | encode time per video |\n|---|---|\n| bundled 4.2.2 | 1.21 s |\n| bundled 4.2.2, `ultrafast` preset | 1.10 s |\n| distribution 6.1.1 (`IMAGEIO_FFMPEG_EXE=/usr/bin/ffmpeg`) | 0.42 s |\n\nEnd to end, that is about 0.6 s per video, or roughly 6% of a 9.9 s request. Grace-based systems (GH200, GB200) are aarch64 too.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDocs only. `performance-optimization.mdx` gets a short \"FFmpeg binary for MP4 encoding\" section. It explains why the bundled binary is pinned, shows how to point `imageio-ffmpeg` at another binary with `IMAGEIO_FFMPEG_EXE`, and states the tradeoff. The default behavior does not change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo code change. In the run above, only the MP4 encode differs: decoded frames are identical, the PSNR between the two encodes is 42 dB or higher, and the file sizes are the same.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Update documentation as needed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41678192341](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41678192341)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41678192409](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41678192409)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
